.DS_Store

# Two of the checks drive a real browser -- check-glsl compiles the shader and
# compares it to the JS per point, check-viewer screenshots both halves of a
# scene -- so running them installs Playwright here. `check-glsl.mjs` looks for
# it at ./node_modules/playwright, which is why it lands in the repository root
# rather than anywhere tidier.
#
# It is not a dependency of anything this repository ships. The kernel has
# none: no bundler, no build step for consumers, and no package.json, which is
# why that file is ignored too rather than committed -- npm writes one as a
# side effect of the install and it describes nothing.
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json
